# Quarto's Jupyter engine executes this document's code blocks, and by default
# it resolves an interpreter of its own -- often one that knows nothing about
# your project's package. Every table and figure in this publication is
# executed code (see report.qmd), so the interpreter is named here rather than
# discovered.
#
# Repo-relative, not absolute. This file sits in report/, so the path is
# resolved from there. An absolute path would bake one machine's filesystem
# into a committed file.
#
# This assumes a uv project with its virtualenv at the repo root (.venv/). If
# yours lives elsewhere, point this at that interpreter instead.
QUARTO_PYTHON=../.venv/bin/python
